       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline in adults, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in their profile explains the higher dose. At doses this high, the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n\n1. **Enter 200 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n2. **Enter a different dose.** For example, I could start at 50 mg daily and titrate up, which is typical.\n3. **Enter 400 mg daily as written.** This is an intentional off-label dose. If so, confirm that it's intended, and I'll add a note to the order such as \"dose exceeds labeled max; intentional per attending.\"\n\nIf 400 mg was a typo, such as 40 mg or 100 mg, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it."
      }
